From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 04:44:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: m4: learn the swap_pace floor outside
 video only

swap_pace learns its lead as the shortest start-to-completion time of
recent swaps that were not held. While a video plays, the swaps that
are not held are its frames that came too late to be held. They arrive
at one phase of the 4.17 ms tick, not spread over it, so the shortest
of a window of them is not the firmware's floor: measured on the J604
during a 60 fps video, the learned lead went from 0.24 ms to 2.1 ms in
one window, and the following held frames then started a tick too
early and showed on the tick between two refreshes.

Learn only from swaps the video gate did not take: animation,
scrolling and input start at every phase of the tick. While a video
plays, the floor learned before it is kept.

Fixes: 8a1452c4fae4 ("drm/apple: m4: learn the swap_pace floor with swap_pace on")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 33c78971c7f59e809c061ea8926f0a1951cf097f)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
index e71aaa5ac9..8a4bf14425 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb_m4.c
@@ -1136,6 +1136,8 @@ struct dcp_m4_runtime {
 	u64 int_start_cnt;
 	/* The swap in flight was held by swap_pace (its start time overstates the floor). */
 	bool int_held;
+	/* The swap in flight was taken for video by swap_pace, held or not. */
+	bool int_gated;
 	u64 int_lat_min;
 	u64 int_lat_win;
 	u32 int_lat_n;
@@ -1815,9 +1817,15 @@ static void dcp_m4_pace_learn(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	 * A held swap starts on purpose well before the tick it aims at, so
 	 * its start-to-completion time overstates the floor, and a window of
 	 * them would raise the estimate by up to a tick each time. Learn from
-	 * swaps that were not held only.
+	 * swaps that were not held only. Nor from the video frames that came
+	 * too late to be held: they arrive at one phase of the tick, so their
+	 * start-to-completion times are not spread over it, and a window of
+	 * them raised the estimate from 0.24 to 2.1 ms in the middle of a
+	 * 60 fps video (measured), which then held the next frames by a tick
+	 * too little. Swaps outside video (animation, scrolling, input) start
+	 * at every phase.
 	 */
-	if (r->int_held)
+	if (r->int_held || r->int_gated)
 		return;
 	lat = done - start;
 	if (!r->int_lat_n || lat < r->int_lat_win)
@@ -2715,6 +2723,7 @@ static unsigned long dcp_m4_swap_pace_us(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	u64 freq, half, margin, base, now, lead, k, start;
 	unsigned int lead_us, min_us;
 
+	r->int_gated = false;
 	if (!READ_ONCE(swap_pace))
 		return 0;
 	WRITE_ONCE(r->pace_e, 0);
@@ -2724,6 +2733,7 @@ static unsigned long dcp_m4_swap_pace_us(struct dcp_m4_runtime *r)
 	min_us = READ_ONCE(swap_pace_min_us);
 	if (min_us && READ_ONCE(r->int_iv_ewma) < div_u64(freq * min_us, USEC_PER_SEC))
 		return 0;
+	r->int_gated = true;
 	half = div_u64(freq, 240);
 	margin = half / 4;
 	base = READ_ONCE(r->int_done_cnt);
-- 
2.43.0

